# Scarab local dev environment (ADR-0036: cluster-free laptop loop).
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and let direnv export it on `cd`:
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#   direnv allow
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored — put machine-specific values (and any
# SCARAB_MASTER_KEY) there, not here. With these set, both dev processes need
# no flags:
#
#   just server   # cargo run -p scarab-server
#   just ui       # vite dev server on http://localhost:5173

# --- scarab-server ---------------------------------------------------------
# Bind to loopback on the dev port the UI proxies to (see ui/scarab-web-ui/vite.config.ts).
SCARAB_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8899

# Durable store. Migrations (incl. 0016/0017) run on connect.
SCARAB_DATABASE_URL=postgres://thulasiram@localhost:5432/scarab_dev

# Host-process executor — no kind/k8s cluster required for laptop runs.
SCARAB_EXECUTOR=local

# Optional: a base64 32-byte key so encrypted secrets survive a server
# restart. Omit and a random ephemeral key is used each boot.
#   SCARAB_MASTER_KEY=$(head -c 32 /dev/urandom | base64)
# SCARAB_MASTER_KEY=

# --- ui --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Point Vite's /v1 proxy at the server above. Only needed if you change
# SCARAB_ADDR from the default dev port.
# SCARAB_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8899
